  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">Parentum <i>vero appellatione intelligi-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>tur etiam:</i> Tutores &amp; Curatores, Pra-</l>
    <l n="3">eceptores, Patres <i>ac</i> Matres-familiás,</l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>uti</i> Liberorum <i>nomine:</i> Pupilli &amp; Cli-</l>
    <l n="5">entes, Discipuli, Domestici. <i>Quatenus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>illi his Parentum, hi vero illis Liberorum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>instar, sunt &amp; esse debent.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8" para="true">Ethica <i>tandem gubernatio attenditur:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>inter</i> seniores &amp; juniores.</l>
    <l n="10" para="true">Seniores <i>hic dicuntur, non tam qui an-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>nis sunt superiores; quam qui donis excel-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>lentibus alios praecellunt: maxime in sacro</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Ministerio. Quod de</i> junioribus <i>ex ad-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>verso etiam notandum.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15" para="true">Illorum <i>officium est, admonitionibus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>&amp; vita exemplo inferiores ad bonam fru-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>gem formare.</i> 1 Tim.5.v.17. Tit.2.v.2.</l>
    <l n="18" para="true">Horum <i>autem, observantia &amp; honore</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>debito superiores profequi, unde καλοζηλία</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>&amp; studium bonos imitandi.</i> Levit.19.v.32.</l>
    <l n="21">Luc.14.v.8.Philip.2.v.3.</l>
    <l n="22" para="true">
      <i>Cum hoc igitur praecepto pugnat: &amp;</i> su-</l>
    <l n="23">periorum &amp; inferiorum vitia.</l>
    <l n="24" para="true">Superiorum <i>vitia sunt: 1. Ἀσωπία,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>maxime in parentibus.</i> 1 Tim.5.v.8. 2.Ni-</l>
    <l n="26">mia indulgentia. 1 Sam.2.v.22-1 Reg.1.v.6.</l>
    <l n="27" para="true">Ni-</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Greek word in the line "unde" rendered from the scan as καλοζηλία; the Greek after "Superiorum" as printed is Ασορνία, read with doubt. The catchword "Ni-" at the foot is taken as a catchword.</notes>
